tions/patient-safety-update/patient-safety-update-april-2024-october-2024/perioperative-anaphylaxis/"], "learning_objective_ids": [5], "hint": {"mode": "eliminate_two_wrong_answers", "eliminate_choices": ["c", "d"], "remaining_choices": ["a", "b"]}}, {"module_id": "course_1_module_4", "question_id": "nmba_11", "question_number": 11, "stem": "For rocuronium block, when is neostigmine a reasonable ASA-guideline alternative to sugammadex?", "choice_a": "When no PTC response is present", "choice_b": "At any depth if the dose is large enough", "choice_c": "At minimal block with quantitative TOF ratio 0.4 to less than 0.9", "choice_d": "When there are two twitches, which always means minimal block", "correct_choice": "c", "rationale": "Minimal block is defined by the quantitative ratio, not merely a twitch count. ASA recommends no more than 40 mcg/kg at minimal block; lower doses may suffice above a ratio of 0.6.", "source_ids": [2], "source_urls": ["https://csa-online.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/02/NMB23.pdf"], "learning_objective_ids": [3, 4], "hint": {"mode": "eliminate_two_wrong_answers", "eliminate_choices": ["b", "d"], "remaining_choices": ["a", "c"]}}, {"module_id": "course_1_module_4", "question_id": "nmba_12", "question_number": 12, "stem": "No TOF twitches are present and the PTC is 1\u20132 after rocuronium. What is the labeled sugammadex dose?", "choice_a": "1 mg/kg IV", "choice_b": "2 mg/kg IV", "choice_c": "16 mg/kg IV in every such case", "choice_d": "4 mg/kg IV", "correct_choice": "d", "rationale": "The labeled deep-block dose is 4 mg/kg when 1\u20132 post-tetanic counts are present with no TOF response. The 16-mg/kg regimen is a separate, specific immediate-reversal circumstance.", "source_ids": [1], "source_urls": ["https://www.merck.com/product/usa/pi_circulars/b/bridion/bridion_pi.pdf"], "learning_objective_ids": [4], "hint": {"mode": "eliminate_two_wrong_answers", "eliminate_choices": ["b", "c"], "remaining_choices": ["a", "d"]}}, {"module_id": "cours