d plasma cholinesterase activity as the depolarizing mechanism", "correct_choice": "a", "rationale": "Depolarization can cause fasciculations and potassium release. Reduced plasma cholinesterase activity instead affects drug clearance and can prolong paralysis.", "source_ids": [4], "source_urls": ["https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=488e1689-84d4-4f96-ac85-fa0cbc661cb6"], "learning_objective_ids": [1, 2], "hint": {"mode": "eliminate_two_wrong_answers", "eliminate_choices": ["c", "d"], "remaining_choices": ["a", "b"]}}, {"module_id": "course_1_module_4", "question_id": "nmba_18", "question_number": 18, "stem": "A 70-kg adult needs reversal about three minutes after a single 1.2-mg/kg rocuronium dose. What dose matches the labeled immediate-reversal regimen?", "choice_a": "140 mg IV", "choice_b": "1,120 mg IV", "choice_c": "280 mg IV", "choice_d": "560 mg IV", "correct_choice": "b", "rationale": "The specified adult regimen is 16 mg/kg: 70 \u00d7 16 = 1,120 mg. It does not guarantee airway patency and must not delay emergency oxygenation or airway rescue.", "source_ids": [1], "source_urls": ["https://www.merck.com/product/usa/pi_circulars/b/bridion/bridion_pi.pdf"], "learning_objective_ids": [4], "hint": {"mode": "eliminate_two_wrong_answers", "eliminate_choices": ["c", "d"], "remaining_choices": ["a", "b"]}}, {"module_id": "course_1_module_4", "question_id": "nmba_19", "question_number": 19, "stem": "Clinically significant bradycardia with a pulse occurs soon after sugammadex. Which response is appropriate?", "choice_a": "Ignore it because sugammadex cannot cause bradycardia", "choice_b": "Give only another NMBA", "choice_c": "Treat promptly, including an anticholinergic such as atropine, with monitoring and escalation if needed", "choice_d": "Use atropine alone even if cardiac arrest develops", "correct_choice": "c", "rationale": "The label recommends an anticholinergic such as atropine for clinically significant bradycardia. Pulseless deterioration requires the appropriate arrest algorithm.", "source_ids": [1], "source_urls": ["https://www.merck.com/product/usa/pi_circulars/b/bridion/bridion_pi.pdf"], "learning_objective_ids": [4, 5], "hint": {"mode": "eliminate_two_wrong_answers", "eliminate_choices": ["b", "d"], "remaining_choices": ["a", "c"]}}, {"module_id": "course_1_module_4", "question_id": "nmba_20", "question_number": 20, "stem": "A retrospective comparison reports no statistically significant mortality difference between two intubation drugs. What is the safest interpretation?", "choice_a": "Both drugs are proven equally safe for every patient", "choice_b": "All succinylcholine contraindications are removed", "choice_c": "Monitoring is unnecessary if group mortality was similar", "choice_d": "The finding does not prove equivalence or override patient-specific contraindications", "correct_choice": "d", "rationale": "Statistical nonsignificance in an observational study is not proof of equivalence. Drug-label contraindications and the individual clinical situation remain decisive.", "source_ids": [4], "source_urls": ["https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=488e1689-84d4-4f96-ac85-fa0cbc661cb6"], "learning_objective_ids": [2, 5], "hint": {"mode": "eliminate_two_wrong_answers", "eliminate_choices": ["b", "c"], "remaining_choices": ["a", "d"]}}, {"module_id": "course_1_module_4", "question_id": "nmba_21", "question_number": 21, "stem": "Chronic phenytoin therapy may have which effect on rocuronium requirements?", "choice_a": "Resistance or shortened duration may occur", "choice_b": "It uniformly causes profound prolonged paralysis", "choice_c": "It makes quantitative monitoring unnecessary", "choice_d": "It converts rocuronium into a depolarizing blocker", "correct_choice": "a", "rationale": "Chronic anticonvulsant exposure can decrease aminosteroid blocker effect or duration. Titrate to measured response rather than assuming all interacting drugs potentiate blockade.", "source_ids